WEBVTT

00:11.094 --> 00:13.513
<i>This is the gigantic floating
fortress that appeared out of nowhere</i>

00:13.596 --> 00:14.764
<i>10,000 meters above ground.</i>

00:14.848 --> 00:18.059
<i>Its appearance marks
the beginning of the neverending war</i>

00:18.143 --> 00:19.686
<i>between humans and monsters.</i>

01:06.649 --> 01:09.486
We are the Divine Dragon Rangers,
the Dragon Keepers!

01:12.072 --> 01:15.700
<i>The Dragon Keepers versus
the Nefarious Monster Army!</i>

01:16.618 --> 01:18.369
<i>It's been 13 years since the battle began,</i>

01:18.453 --> 01:21.456
<i>and the weekly Sunday Showdown
continues to draw a huge crowd.</i>

01:22.082 --> 01:25.126
<i>What kind of fierce battle
awaits us today?</i>

01:25.210 --> 01:27.337
I can't wait to find out!

01:27.921 --> 01:29.798
<i>The Rangers appear to be
on a state of high alert</i>

01:29.881 --> 01:32.300
<i>in the midst of all the excitement
and tension!</i>

01:32.634 --> 01:34.219
<i>Monster experts predict</i>

01:34.302 --> 01:38.098
that the monster army has a high chance
of deploying their secret weapon

01:38.181 --> 01:39.516
in today's showdown!

01:40.892 --> 01:44.437
<i>Whoa! The Red Keeper is here
to greet everyone first!</i>

01:44.521 --> 01:46.106
Thank you very much!

01:47.398 --> 01:48.775
Zoom in! Zoom in!

01:50.610 --> 01:52.320
<i>He takes good care of his fans.</i>

01:52.403 --> 01:54.447
<i>As expected of
the chief of the Ranger Force.</i>

01:54.531 --> 01:57.117
- <i>The Dragon Keeper's reliable leader!</i>
- Please don't push, all right?

01:57.200 --> 02:00.203
<i>Will we witness his ultimate
technique, the Dragon Slash, today?</i>

02:00.286 --> 02:02.956
<i>As usual, we'll entrust
humanity's future to them this week.</i>

02:03.039 --> 02:05.750
<i>And as for the Monster Army,
they have yet to be sighted.</i>

02:05.834 --> 02:08.920
<i>Just what could they be up to
at the floating fortress far away...</i>

02:13.341 --> 02:15.343
Are you here to spectate the fight?

02:15.426 --> 02:17.178
This place will turn
into a battlefield soon.

02:17.262 --> 02:21.015
We'll do our very best
to ensure your safety!

02:22.350 --> 02:25.103
But if you insist
on spectating despite the risks,

02:25.186 --> 02:26.229
then feel free to proceed.

02:31.609 --> 02:37.448
Oh, come on... Risks? There haven't been
any civilian casualties in years, right?

02:37.532 --> 02:39.701
It's part of our protocol to say that.

02:39.784 --> 02:41.035
What?

02:42.287 --> 02:44.080
How admirable.

02:44.164 --> 02:46.791
You're both so young, yet you're already
part of the Ranger Force.

02:46.875 --> 02:48.293
You can do it too!

02:48.376 --> 02:51.296
The Ranger Force is always
looking out for new blood!

02:51.379 --> 02:53.756
- Please! Join us!
- H-Hey, you're too close! Too close!

02:56.050 --> 02:58.469
We are recruiting!!
The Dragon Keepers

02:59.012 --> 03:00.388
Mm.

03:00.471 --> 03:02.473
Me, joining the Ranger Force?

03:02.557 --> 03:04.976
It's not that hard, really.

03:05.560 --> 03:08.479
But whether you'll be like
those guys is another story.

03:15.904 --> 03:19.073
The rest is up to you, I guess.

03:30.418 --> 03:32.629
All right. This way, please.

04:06.704 --> 04:10.625
Strike your victory pose

04:40.321 --> 04:41.489
The monsters are here!

04:41.572 --> 04:44.200
They just don't learn,
do they? They keep coming back!

04:44.284 --> 04:47.161
We won't lose! Just get lost already!

04:47.745 --> 04:51.666
- Get lost! Get lost! Get lost!
- Get lost! Get lost! Get lost!

04:52.667 --> 04:54.085
Ow, that hurt!

04:54.919 --> 04:56.087
Ouch!

04:57.630 --> 04:59.132
There you are, monsters!

04:59.215 --> 05:00.258
What?

05:06.556 --> 05:07.890
So you've come.

05:10.059 --> 05:12.103
We won't let you have your way.

05:12.729 --> 05:15.398
This planet belongs to us humans!

05:15.481 --> 05:17.692
And we will protect it
from the likes of you!

05:22.739 --> 05:23.823
We are...

05:23.906 --> 05:26.075
- ...the Dragon Keepers!
- ...the Dragon Keepers!

05:30.496 --> 05:32.915
Red Keeper
Pink Keeper

05:40.923 --> 05:44.260
I'm a monster born from all
the collective grudges of the tigers

05:44.344 --> 05:45.636
in this world.

05:45.720 --> 05:49.349
You foolish surface-dwellers
shall get what you deserve!

05:49.932 --> 05:53.770
For starters,
I'll turn all animals tiger-striped

05:53.853 --> 05:56.230
and turn this world into absolute chaos!

05:56.314 --> 05:58.983
How dare you! Anything but that!

06:00.818 --> 06:03.446
The heck are you surface-dwellers
looking at?

06:03.529 --> 06:05.615
This isn't a zoo!

06:05.698 --> 06:09.035
Get them, Dusters! Show them hell!

06:10.536 --> 06:11.788
Oh goodness, no!

06:13.706 --> 06:15.124
Stop!

06:20.129 --> 06:21.839
I'll be the one to deal with you.

06:23.049 --> 06:26.052
Sakurama, bring the spectators
somewhere safe.

06:26.135 --> 06:27.512
I'm on it, Suzukiri!

06:27.595 --> 06:30.098
- Come. Right this way.
- Thank you very much!

06:43.569 --> 06:45.696
Come on, now! What's wrong?

06:45.780 --> 06:49.325
Is that all you've got, Dragon Keepers?

06:50.535 --> 06:53.788
This monster is stronger
than any other we've fought before!

06:54.539 --> 06:55.915
It's unbelievably powerful.

06:57.166 --> 06:59.001
If it's a battle of strength
you're looking for,

06:59.085 --> 07:00.837
I, the Green Keeper,
will be your opponent!

07:03.256 --> 07:05.758
H-Hey, wait! Th-That's too big!

07:07.844 --> 07:10.513
Hah! How'd you like that, monster?

07:10.596 --> 07:13.015
Devastating strength!

07:27.530 --> 07:29.782
I knew it'd take more than that
to kill that monster!

07:30.283 --> 07:31.951
Why aren't they using the Divine Artifact?

07:32.034 --> 07:35.705
I will never die. I'm immortal!

07:37.915 --> 07:41.711
Transformation! Tora Tora Toransform!

07:50.178 --> 07:51.804
Scrum!
Got it!

08:09.572 --> 08:10.990
What? This can't be real!

08:11.073 --> 08:13.242
That monster's really strong...

08:13.326 --> 08:16.245
Maybe we're really done for this time.

08:19.081 --> 08:20.333
It's too powerful...

08:21.918 --> 08:24.837
Don't lose, Dragon Keepers!

08:24.921 --> 08:26.130
Get up!

08:26.714 --> 08:28.299
Blast those monsters away!

08:30.801 --> 08:33.554
There's no way... we'll lose.

08:34.597 --> 08:36.766
As long as
there's someone left to protect,

08:37.808 --> 08:41.229
we'll get up on our feet,
no matter how many times!

08:47.276 --> 08:50.112
Yikes! They're using
the Divine Artifact already!

08:50.196 --> 08:52.156
Gather around, surviving Dusters!

08:55.701 --> 08:57.537
We're going with the classic this time.

08:57.620 --> 09:00.373
Right after they fire
the Dragon Blaster, got it?

09:00.456 --> 09:01.749
They'll blast us back into the fortress,

09:01.832 --> 09:03.501
and then we'll reconstruct
ourselves, right?

09:03.584 --> 09:05.628
I'm looking forward
to your loser's speech this time.

09:06.462 --> 09:08.631
Now what do I do? I didn't think of one!

09:08.714 --> 09:10.550
What about "I'll remember this!"?

09:10.633 --> 09:13.010
Sounds like what a monster would say.
Doesn't that sound cool?

09:13.094 --> 09:15.012
Come on. That's too cliche, D.

09:15.096 --> 09:16.722
Wait, Fighter D?

09:16.806 --> 09:18.849
I thought you weren't supposed to be
on shift today!

09:18.933 --> 09:19.934
Uh-huh.

09:20.017 --> 09:22.436
What do you mean, "Uh-huh"?
What are you doing here?

09:22.520 --> 09:23.563
Huh?

09:24.647 --> 09:26.065
- Dragon's Breath!
- Dragon's Breath!

09:26.148 --> 09:28.609
Oh, no, not good! Fortify our defense!

09:28.693 --> 09:30.194
- I'm tired of this already.
- Eh?

09:30.278 --> 09:32.446
I'm sick of putting up with this act.

09:32.530 --> 09:34.490
Wait! Hey, D! Don't go!

09:34.574 --> 09:36.617
Wait! We're almost done!

09:38.536 --> 09:39.704
- Fire!
- Fire!

09:42.790 --> 09:45.042
<i>I'm so done with this pretense.</i>

09:54.552 --> 09:56.596
All done. And now, to the commercials!

10:11.319 --> 10:13.195
We're done for this time!

10:14.947 --> 10:16.073
I can't think of anything.

10:16.157 --> 10:17.658
Don't give up!

10:17.742 --> 10:19.327
No matter what it takes,

10:19.410 --> 10:22.413
we've got to come up
with the monster for this week-- Ow!

10:22.496 --> 10:23.497
Monster of the week

10:23.581 --> 10:26.917
There's no way we can come up
with new ideas every single week!

10:27.710 --> 10:29.587
I'm fresh out of ideas!

10:29.670 --> 10:31.589
Like I care anymore.
I'm going to take a nap.

10:31.672 --> 10:34.675
<i>The Dragon Keepers versus
the Nefarious Monster Army!</i>

10:34.759 --> 10:36.385
<i>It's been 13 years since the battle began,</i>

10:36.469 --> 10:38.846
<i>and the weekly Sunday Showdown
continues to draw a huge crowd.</i>

10:38.929 --> 10:41.057
Hey, seems like
the arena's getting all fired up.

10:41.140 --> 10:43.476
Let's see if he says anything
that'll help serve as a hint.

10:43.559 --> 10:46.312
<i>Monster experts predict that
the monster army</i>

10:46.395 --> 10:49.273
<i>has a high chance
of deploying their secret weapon...</i>

10:49.357 --> 10:51.192
Nope! There's nothing at all!

10:51.275 --> 10:54.403
A 13-year-long battle? Get real!

10:54.487 --> 10:56.447
Why are we even in this mess?

10:56.530 --> 11:01.202
Still, who would've expected this
to happen to us?

11:01.285 --> 11:03.829
<i>The floating fortress fell in just a year,</i>

11:03.913 --> 11:06.707
<i>and all our bosses were wiped out
along with it.</i>

11:06.791 --> 11:10.294
<i>We're just Dusters.
What can foot soldiers like us even do?</i>

11:11.420 --> 11:15.966
Hold on. Our bosses were exterminated,
so why were we left alive?

11:16.050 --> 11:18.678
Who knows? Maybe they chickened out
because there's too many of us.

11:18.761 --> 11:21.472
<i>Whoa! The Red Keeper is here
to greet everyone first!</i>

11:21.555 --> 11:24.058
Wait, this isn't the time for chit-chat!

11:24.141 --> 11:27.645
Oh fine, I'll come up with something then!

11:27.728 --> 11:29.647
- Fighter G!
- Fighter G!

11:31.857 --> 11:35.653
How about this? A super-strong monster
with bulging muscles!

11:36.195 --> 11:37.363
Wow!

11:37.446 --> 11:38.656
It looks strong!

11:38.739 --> 11:40.032
Rejected.

11:40.116 --> 11:41.450
Wh-Why?

11:41.534 --> 11:42.868
I've said this before.

11:42.952 --> 11:46.038
Abstract ideas don't leave
a lasting impression on the audience!

11:46.622 --> 11:49.166
It's going to lose
the moment it steps foot on the stage!

11:49.250 --> 11:51.794
The monster should have
some sort of motif.

11:51.877 --> 11:54.130
You're harsh, Fighter A.

11:54.213 --> 11:56.966
If you get hung up on the details,
we're not going to make it in time!

11:57.049 --> 11:58.050
For goodness' sake!

11:58.134 --> 12:01.303
We wouldn't be in this mess
if our bosses were still alive!

12:01.387 --> 12:03.723
There's no point thinking about
what we don't have!

12:03.806 --> 12:05.933
We'll just have to manage on our own!

12:06.016 --> 12:07.309
- Fighter L!
- Fighter L!

12:08.769 --> 12:11.147
How about this? It's a cute cat monster!

12:11.230 --> 12:14.483
I'm sure the surface-dwellers
will love it. It'll be really popular!

12:14.567 --> 12:16.360
Why would you want them to love it?

12:16.444 --> 12:20.322
We're supposed to create big bad monsters
that strike fear in kids!

12:20.906 --> 12:24.535
There's a sense of catharsis
that comes from defeating scary monsters!

12:24.618 --> 12:26.328
In that case,
we can change it into a lion--

12:26.412 --> 12:28.038
We made a lion seven years ago!

12:30.207 --> 12:31.208
A tiger.

12:31.292 --> 12:32.376
- What?
- What?

12:32.460 --> 12:34.962
I'm pretty sure
we haven't made a tiger yet.

12:35.045 --> 12:37.047
I've heard that on the surface,

12:37.131 --> 12:39.467
they use the dragon and tiger
to describe rivals.

12:40.801 --> 12:42.595
Oh, come on. You're in the way!

12:42.678 --> 12:45.055
If the Dragon Keepers has its roots
in the dragon,

12:45.139 --> 12:47.600
then shouldn't we be the tiger?

12:47.683 --> 12:50.603
You're as conscientious as ever.

12:50.686 --> 12:53.063
The dragon and tiger, huh...

12:53.147 --> 12:54.815
That's making me kind of embarrassed.

12:55.399 --> 12:58.319
I sure hope they think of us that way,
even though we lose every week.

12:59.111 --> 13:00.905
Why are you guys
already thinking of losing?

13:00.988 --> 13:03.824
Huh?
- We're monsters.

13:03.908 --> 13:07.328
We take down anyone in our way,
even the Dragon Keepers! Isn't that right?

13:08.329 --> 13:09.580
We may not win now,

13:09.663 --> 13:12.249
but we can't give up on hoping
that we'll eventually win one day.

13:12.333 --> 13:14.585
That's what's important, don't you agree?

13:14.668 --> 13:16.003
Quiet down, D!

13:16.629 --> 13:18.339
I can't hear the radio!

13:18.422 --> 13:20.299
Don't listen
to the nonsense they say

13:20.382 --> 13:21.801
just to please the surface-dwellers!

13:21.884 --> 13:22.968
Your ears are going to rot!

13:23.052 --> 13:24.595
What we should be doing

13:24.678 --> 13:27.264
is not creating a monster
that'll be defeated today,

13:27.348 --> 13:29.600
but coming up with a strategy
to win today!

13:30.142 --> 13:33.938
At this rate,
we're never going to fulfill our mission!

13:34.021 --> 13:35.314
Mission?

13:35.397 --> 13:36.607
What's our mission?

13:36.690 --> 13:38.859
World domination.

13:38.943 --> 13:41.445
Our bosses may be gone,
but our mission remains the same.

13:41.529 --> 13:45.574
We're supposed to fight
and make this planet ours!

13:46.158 --> 13:49.245
Let's do this!

13:49.829 --> 13:51.956
Round and round...

13:54.542 --> 13:56.293
World domination, he says!

13:56.377 --> 13:58.379
It's been a long time
since I heard that!

13:58.462 --> 14:00.464
As expected of Fighter D!

14:00.548 --> 14:02.216
He's ambitious, I'll give him that!

14:02.299 --> 14:04.510
How conscientious!

14:22.570 --> 14:24.196
Here we go.

14:24.864 --> 14:26.574
You should calm down, D.

14:26.657 --> 14:29.201
What's the point of fighting
amongst ourselves?

14:29.702 --> 14:31.620
Come on, F...

14:32.288 --> 14:34.164
Aren't you mad about this?

14:34.665 --> 14:38.294
We've resigned ourselves to being
satisfied with what we have now.

14:39.295 --> 14:40.713
For the past 13 years,

14:40.796 --> 14:43.007
we've already fought 1,000 times
with the Rangers.

14:43.090 --> 14:44.425
You should know better than that.

14:44.508 --> 14:47.553
Not yet. We've only fought 998 times.

14:47.636 --> 14:49.179
Don't harp on the details.

14:49.263 --> 14:50.556
Listen.

14:50.639 --> 14:53.559
<i>We lost the day
our bosses were exterminated.</i>

14:54.143 --> 14:56.604
<i>We still continue to invade the planet
every Sunday,</i>

14:56.687 --> 14:59.982
<i>but we can't let the civilians know
that this is all just an act.</i>

15:00.774 --> 15:03.736
<i>This is the condition for the truce
we agreed on that very day.</i>

15:04.320 --> 15:07.907
Maybe they don't even think of us
as monsters anymore.

15:08.490 --> 15:10.242
It's time you accept it.

15:12.703 --> 15:13.746
All right.

15:13.829 --> 15:16.790
We had some problems, but I assume
everyone's fine with the tiger.

15:16.874 --> 15:18.918
Come forward if you're good at
acting as a tiger.

15:19.001 --> 15:20.836
Also, give me a copy of
the animal encyclopedia

15:20.920 --> 15:22.087
that the Rangers provided.

15:22.171 --> 15:23.297
Oh, I'll do it.

15:23.380 --> 15:24.590
Fighter Z, right?

15:24.673 --> 15:25.799
World animal encyclopedia

15:25.883 --> 15:27.009
Think you can do it?

15:27.092 --> 15:29.553
Who knows? I'll just have to try.

15:38.896 --> 15:42.900
Not done yet?
Just a little more...

15:44.985 --> 15:46.612
Wait! Hey, come on!

15:47.696 --> 15:51.533
How's this? I don't really know
how a tiger works, so...

15:51.617 --> 15:52.701
Yeah, you look like one.

15:52.785 --> 15:54.453
I think we need
a little oomph.

15:54.536 --> 15:57.081
O-Oh, really? In that case...
Tiger... Tora... Truck.

15:57.164 --> 15:59.833
I'm probably better than him
at reconstruction.

15:59.917 --> 16:01.377
Then you should do it, D.

16:01.460 --> 16:04.922
I'm busy today. Besides, I'm not on shift.

16:05.005 --> 16:08.384
Again? Where have you been off to
all alone lately?

16:10.135 --> 16:11.387
D?

16:11.971 --> 16:13.889
I'd never volunteer as boss.

16:13.973 --> 16:16.058
Not if I'm meant to be defeated.

16:16.141 --> 16:18.560
Huh, so you do know.

16:21.105 --> 16:22.189
Hey, D.

16:22.272 --> 16:23.273
What?

16:23.357 --> 16:25.651
During the last Sunday Showdown,

16:25.734 --> 16:28.278
I saw a small surface-dweller
in front of me.

16:29.822 --> 16:32.616
<i>Can you guess
what he said to me, his enemy?</i>

16:33.867 --> 16:36.036
<i>He said, "Do your best."</i>

16:37.121 --> 16:38.747
I didn't get why he said that to me.

16:38.831 --> 16:40.207
It made no sense, right?

16:45.295 --> 16:48.757
But you know,
it didn't feel half bad for some reason.

16:49.758 --> 16:51.510
I feel like for the sake
of the general public

16:51.593 --> 16:53.971
who don't know the truth,
I have to do my best.

16:55.139 --> 16:59.560
We make the Rangers stand out,
and the audience gets all pumped up.

17:00.394 --> 17:02.688
It doesn't matter
even if I know we're going to lose.

17:10.154 --> 17:11.321
- Fire!
- Fire!

17:13.907 --> 17:17.077
<i>I'll do my best to play
the perfect monster.</i>

17:21.165 --> 17:24.293
There it is! Their ultimate technique,
the Dragon's Breath!

17:24.376 --> 17:26.253
<i>Once again, the future of humanity</i>

17:26.336 --> 17:28.922
<i>has been protected
by the Dragon Keepers this week!</i>

17:30.549 --> 17:31.759
That freaking hurt.

17:31.842 --> 17:33.010
Just because we're immortal,

17:33.093 --> 17:35.179
doesn't mean that
you can do whatever you want to us.

17:35.262 --> 17:37.264
We can still feel pain, you know.

17:37.347 --> 17:40.350
Monsters aren't meant
to just take a beating.

17:40.934 --> 17:43.937
Even though the civilians don't realize
that this is just an act,

17:44.021 --> 17:47.107
we're just repeating the same thing
every single week.

17:47.691 --> 17:49.735
Are you guys really satisfied with this?

17:49.818 --> 17:51.904
Don't you want more?

17:51.987 --> 17:56.283
How about something different
for a change?

17:57.117 --> 17:59.620
The possibility
of the monsters winning, that is.

18:02.247 --> 18:03.499
It seems like we missed one.

18:04.208 --> 18:07.544
Come on. This isn't what we agreed on.

18:07.628 --> 18:09.797
Look at that fool!

18:09.880 --> 18:11.882
Hey, isn't this bad?

18:12.466 --> 18:16.386
Hey! You can still make it
in time, so get back to the fortress now!

18:17.221 --> 18:19.389
It's time to...

18:19.973 --> 18:21.433
end the rigged games.

18:23.227 --> 18:25.896
I'll take you guys down...

18:26.647 --> 18:31.151
with a real fight!

18:34.029 --> 18:35.364
He's running over.

18:35.447 --> 18:36.532
What a pain.

18:37.032 --> 18:38.325
Perhaps I should deal with him.

18:38.408 --> 18:39.910
It's all up to you, Red!

18:44.331 --> 18:46.542
What a courageous fighter!

18:46.625 --> 18:48.669
You seem like a formidable opponent!

18:51.380 --> 18:53.298
All right! Finally someone with guts!

18:53.882 --> 18:54.883
You can do it!

18:54.967 --> 18:55.968
<i>What?</i>

18:57.803 --> 18:59.221
Monster!

18:59.304 --> 19:01.974
Monster! Do your best!

19:02.057 --> 19:03.308
W-Whoa!

19:03.392 --> 19:05.727
<i>I get it already, so just shut up.</i>

19:05.811 --> 19:08.147
<i>You guys just want to see a trash mob</i>

19:08.230 --> 19:10.649
<i>struggle and get beaten up
pathetically, right?</i>

19:10.732 --> 19:12.985
<i>Screw this. Don't look down on me!</i>

19:13.068 --> 19:17.030
<i>I'll make those stupid,
ignorant faces of yours twitch with fear!</i>

19:17.114 --> 19:21.451
<i>Take a good look.
The one you see before your eyes...</i>

19:21.535 --> 19:26.248
is a big, bad, and proud monster!

19:26.331 --> 19:28.041
All right, good job today.

19:28.876 --> 19:30.586
Don't get too ahead of yourself.

19:31.086 --> 19:33.630
This isn't the stage
for your kind to shine.

19:33.714 --> 19:35.799
Just shut up and lose
like you're supposed to.

19:35.883 --> 19:38.552
Read the situation and know your place.

19:39.219 --> 19:41.597
We are justice!

19:46.894 --> 19:48.312
- Fire!
- Fire!

19:50.898 --> 19:52.191
<i>I've had enough.</i>

19:52.774 --> 19:55.110
<i>I don't even look like a bad guy now.</i>

20:01.909 --> 20:05.120
Fighter M got blasted off by the wind.

20:05.204 --> 20:06.330
Good work.

20:06.413 --> 20:10.918
This makes 999 battles
and 999 losses, huh?

20:11.001 --> 20:12.336
Why think about that now?

20:13.045 --> 20:16.006
Why isn't D back yet?

20:16.423 --> 20:17.591
Not surprising.

20:18.175 --> 20:20.677
<i>Many like him ran off because
they couldn't stand this anymore.</i>

20:20.761 --> 20:25.265
<i>Doing what they tell us to do
is the only way for us to survive.</i>

20:30.562 --> 20:32.397
<i>Now I know.</i>

20:33.023 --> 20:35.817
<i>No, I've always known.</i>

20:36.568 --> 20:39.029
<i>We aren't even fit to be the villains.</i>

20:39.613 --> 20:41.782
<i>At this rate,
we'll just continue to be their slaves.</i>

20:42.699 --> 20:46.245
I'm sick of staying silent
and doing their bidding!

20:47.204 --> 20:48.372
Oh?

20:48.455 --> 20:50.624
You surprised me.
You're the one we met in the morning!

20:50.707 --> 20:52.709
What are you doing here?

20:53.210 --> 20:57.631
I wanted a better view of the battlefield
from a higher place, so...

20:57.714 --> 20:59.549
Mm. Isn't it great?

20:59.633 --> 21:01.468
I like this spot too.

21:02.052 --> 21:03.971
So, how was it?

21:04.054 --> 21:06.556
What do you think about
the Sunday Showdown?

21:07.557 --> 21:11.520
Well, I guess it was amazing
to see the Dragon Keepers up close.

21:12.354 --> 21:13.563
They're strong.

21:13.647 --> 21:15.440
In fact, they're really strong.

21:18.026 --> 21:20.195
I want to be like them too.

21:20.696 --> 21:21.697
Oh?

21:21.780 --> 21:24.324
Can I take it that you're interested
in joining the Rangers?

21:25.867 --> 21:27.452
That sounds like a good idea.

21:27.536 --> 21:30.080
In fact, maybe I should take
the recruitment exam!

21:31.164 --> 21:33.625
Looks like you're all fired up now.

21:34.167 --> 21:35.168
Yeah.

21:40.674 --> 21:42.134
I'll take them down.

21:42.217 --> 21:44.511
I'll defeat all our enemies.

21:45.178 --> 21:47.472
<i>Despite the Dragon Keepers'
desperate struggle</i>

21:47.556 --> 21:49.433
<i>against the monster boss'
devastating strength,</i>

21:49.516 --> 21:53.895
<i>the cheers from the public
sparked a surge of power within them!</i>

21:53.979 --> 21:58.108
<i>The victory of humanity is within reach!
Fight on, Dragon Keepers!</i>

21:58.191 --> 22:00.610
<i>Protect our planet!</i>

23:28.907 --> 23:30.909
Translated by Qianni Lu

23:31.993 --> 23:34.329
"Go! Fighter D!"

23:34.413 --> 23:36.498
- Sounds good. Let's go with that.
-"Go"? Where are you going?

23:36.581 --> 23:38.208
I'm not going anywhere!
I'm short on time, so shoo!

23:38.291 --> 23:39.292
What were you saying?

23:39.376 --> 23:40.460
Shut it! I'm just doing it!

23:40.544 --> 23:41.545
Just what is it?

23:41.628 --> 23:43.839
Next episode, "Go! Fighter D!"

23:43.922 --> 23:45.507
<i>All right, that sounded really awesome.</i>

23:45.590 --> 23:46.925
You were talking about the episode title?
